.TH INTERNETIP 1 "2026-04-14" "internetip 2.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
internetip \- fetch and display the public internet IP address
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B internetip
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B internetip
.I command
[\fIargument\fR]
.br
.B source internetip
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B internetip
fetches the current public IP address from
.I https://ipecho.net/plain
using
.BR curl (1)
with automatic retry (3 attempts, 5-second delay). The fetched address is
validated by
.BR validip (1)
before being printed. When invoked as root, the result is cached to
.I $GATEWAY_IP_FILE
(default
.IR /tmp/GatewayIP ).
.PP
With
.BR \-s ", " \-c ", or " \-\-call\-url ,
.B internetip
additionally calls a configured callback URL after fetching the IP,
suitable for dynamic DNS registration, server inventory updates, and
automated IP notification workflows. The callback URL supports runtime
template variables (see
.B URL TEMPLATE VARIABLES
below). Callback requests use full TLS certificate verification.
.PP
When sourced as a Bash module,
.B internetip
exports the
.B get_internet_ip
function and also makes
.BR valid_ip ,
.BR valid_ip4 ,
and
.B valid_ip6
available (lazy-loaded from
.BR validip (1)).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Install
.BR internetip ", " validip ", and " watchip
as symlinks in
.IR /usr/local/bin ,
plus per-script bash completion files in
.IR /etc/bash_completion.d .
Requires root.
.TP
.B update
.BR "git pull"
the repository directory and reinstall. Requires root.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove installed symlinks and completion files. Requires root.
.TP
.BR "seturl " [\fIurl\fR]
Configure the system-wide callback URL template. Writes
.I $INTERNETIP_PROFILE
(default
.IR /etc/profile.d/internetip.sh )
and
.IR /etc/systemd/system-environment-generators/internetip .
Prompts interactively if no URL is given. Requires root. URLs are escaped
for shell-safe embedding before being written. Also accepts the form
.BR seturl= \fIurl\fR.
.TP
.B showurl
Show the current callback URL template and its expanded form.
.TP
.B unseturl
Remove the system-wide URL configuration. Requires root.
.PP
Long-option forms
.RB ( \-\-install ", " \-\-update ", " \-\-uninstall ", " \-\-set\-url ", "
.BR \-\-show\-url ", " \-\-unset\-url )
are also accepted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-c ", " \-\-call\-url
After fetching the IP, call the configured
.I $INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
template (with variables expanded).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational output. Warnings and errors still display.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End-of-options sentinel.
.PP
Short options may be bundled:
.B \-cv
is equivalent to
.B \-c \-v
and
.BR \-sv
to
.BR "\-s \-v" .
.SH URL TEMPLATE VARIABLES
Callback URLs may contain template tokens that are substituted at runtime.
The
.B $
prefix is optional (\fBHOSTNAME\fR works the same as \fB$HOSTNAME\fR):
.TP
.B HOSTNAME
The system hostname (from
.BR hostname (1)).
.TP
.B GATEWAY_IP
The currently fetched public IP.
.TP
.B WIFI
The active Wi-Fi SSID, resolved via
.BR iwgetid (8)
and
.BR nmcli (1)
in order. Falls back to
.B HOSTNAME
if neither tool is installed or no network is active.
.TP
.B SCRIPT_NAME
The script basename
.RB ( internetip ).
.TP
.B VERSION
The script version string.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
Callback URL template for the
.B \-s
option. Normally set via
.B seturl
and sourced from
.I $INTERNETIP_PROFILE
on login, or emitted by the systemd environment generator for system
services.
.TP
.B INTERNETIP_PROFILE
Path to the shell profile fragment that exports
.B INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
on login. Default:
.IR /etc/profile.d/internetip.sh .
.TP
.B GATEWAY_IP_FILE
Path to the root-written cache file. Default:
.IR /tmp/GatewayIP .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B internetip
uses the BCS0602 canonical exit-code vocabulary:
.TP
.B 0
Success \- IP retrieved (and callback invoked if requested).
.TP
.B 3
ERR_NOENT \- script file missing or unreadable path during
.BR install / update .
.TP
.B 13
ERR_ACCESS \- operation requires root.
.TP
.B 18
ERR_NODEP \-
.BR validip (1)
dependency unreachable.
.TP
.B 19
ERR_CONFIG \-
.B INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
not configured.
.TP
.B 21
ERR_STATE \- repository directory is not a git checkout
(during
.BR update ).
.TP
.B 22
ERR_INVAL \- unknown option or unexpected argument.
.TP
.B 23
ERR_NETWORK \- IP fetch failed, callback URL failed, or
.B git pull
failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/internetip.sh
Login-shell export of
.B INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
(written by
.BR seturl ).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system-environment-generators/internetip
Systemd environment generator that emits
.B INTERNETIP_CALL_URL
for system services (written by
.BR seturl ).
.TP
.I /tmp/GatewayIP
Cached public IP, written when
.B internetip
is run as root.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display the current public IP:
.PP
.EX
internetip
.EE
.PP
Configure a callback URL (interactively) and then use it:
.PP
.EX
sudo internetip seturl
# Enter: https://example.com/ip.php?host=HOSTNAME&ip=GATEWAY_IP
internetip -s
.EE
.PP
Pass the URL directly:
.PP
.EX
sudo internetip seturl='https://example.com?host=HOSTNAME&ip=GATEWAY_IP'
.EE
.PP
When invoking via SSH, encode
.B &
as
.B %26
to survive intermediate shell parsing:
.PP
.EX
ssh host "internetip seturl='https://example.com?host=HOSTNAME%26ip=GATEWAY_IP'"
.EE
.PP
Use as a Bash module:
.PP
.EX
source internetip
ip=$(get_internet_ip)
echo "Current IP: $ip"
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR validip (1),
.BR watchip (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR systemd.environment-generator (7),
.BR iwgetid (8),
.BR nmcli (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Biksu Okusi <biksu@okusi.id>
